                 fair (n=1,079). Familiarity before voting: 45 per cent had
                 heard of it and understood it, 44 were very familiar, 10 had
                 heard of it but did not understand it, 2 had never heard of it
                 (n=1,061). Use of RCV: 49 per cent in every election, 39 not
                 at all, 7 primaries only, 4 not enough knowledge to say, 1
                 general and special only (n=1,044). Respondents were 73 per
                 cent White (n=1,000), 73 per cent homeowners (n=1,029) and 43
                 per cent aged 60 or over (n=1,032). Two questions have no 2023
                 counterpart: whether the respondent had voted in a previous
