  note        = {Chs. 610 and 611, Acts of the General Assembly of Virginia,
                 session of 1952, printed p. 1063, both approved 3 April 1952
                 [H 743 and H 744]},
  annotation  = {Two administrative acts of 3 April 1952, printed together. Ch.
                 610 re-enacts sec. 15-353.1: the Board by resolution "may
                 require the county manager, auditor and attorney for the
                 Commonwealth to certify to the treasurer the payroll of the
                 regular employees of the county" and vouchers for bills
                 carrying a discount, and the treasurer then pays them "as if
                 they had been approved by the county board", subject to
                 certification to the Board at its next meeting and to any
                 Board resolution opposing the method. Ch. 611 adds sec.
                 15-354.1, creating a department of real estate assessments:
                 "If a majority of the voters voting in a referendum as
                 hereinafter provided vote for the establishment of a
                 department of real estate assessments, the county board shall
                 by ordinance establish such department". That referendum was
                 held with the two County Manager Act questions and carried
                 17,795 to 11,348 on 4 November 1952 (dailysun1952results),
                 which is why the 1952 package was wider than the three acts
                 that print questions. Filed in Drive as "legal/state
