                 the Circuit Court ruling that the Board should appoint
                 department heads. Both are filed and neither is preferred
                 here; they may also describe different things, since the
                 statute before 1952 gave the Board department-head selection
                 while the police chief sat under the Public Safety Director.
                 The rest of the page is the occasion: applications for chief
                 were being taken from county policemen until noon Monday, the
                 post having been vacant "Since March 1, when H. L. lY°° d y«
                 rd retired" (the OCR of Woodyard); County Manager A. T.
                 Lundberg asked all fourteen captains, lieutenants and
